# Next.js web source layout

Follow `apps/web/AGENTS.md`. Next.js **App Router** (not Vite / React Router). pnpm. API is Nest on **3001**.

When the first feature lands, use `src/app` (not package-root `app/`). `@/` → `src/`.

## Folder split

```
apps/web/src/
  app/           # routes + page-local components/ and hooks/
  components/    # shared UI only (2+ routes), no fetch
  shared/hooks/  # shared client hooks (2+ routes)
  module/        # repository, dtos; use-case only with business logic
  infra/         # HTTP client only
  utils/         # pure helpers
```

Do not add `src/app/api` CRUD proxies. Do not put Keycloak or `fetch` inside components.

## Feature module (`src/module/<entity>/`)

- `{entity}.repository.ts` — one HTTP verb per method
- `use-case/{kebab-name}.ts` — multi-step / validated writes only; do not wrap a single repository call
- `{entity}-module.ts` — `new XRepository(apiClient)`
- Results: `Result<ApiSuccess<T>, ApiError>` (neverthrow). No `try/catch` fetch. UI: `getApiErrorMessage`.

Pages are thin Server Components by default. `'use client'` only for events, browser APIs, or hooks. Server Actions only wrap use-cases or repositories.

Colocate page-only UI and hooks under `src/app/{segment}/`. Lift UI to `src/components` or hooks to `src/shared/hooks` only when a second route needs them. Do not put hooks in `src/module`.

Copy the nearest sibling. Entities follow the API: `auth`, `users`, `articles`, `video`, …
